Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:48:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Count a weapon at what it was worth in 1.8

1.8 built a weapon's damage from a base for its kind plus the material's
bonus: 4 for a sword, 3 for an axe, 2 for a pickaxe and 1 for a shovel.
The bonuses are unchanged, the bases are not, so a diamond sword hit for
8 there and 7 now, and a diamond axe for 7 there and 9 now.

The swap happens where a melee hit reads the attack damage attribute, for
players and for mobs alike, as 1.8 applied the same item modifiers to
both. The item registry is left as it is, so the change follows a reload,
nothing stored or sent changes, and a weapon with modifiers of its own
keeps them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
index dd5078c5d11e602588606eb3715e3a7d6a4f5487..225a52c36ce301541bd86b9a0670cf14080a1733 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/entity/Mob.java
@@ -1632,7 +1632,7 @@ public abstract class Mob extends LivingEntity implements Targeting, EquipmentUs
 
     @Override
     public boolean doHurtTarget(final ServerLevel level, final Entity target) {
-        float dmg = (float)this.getAttributeValue(Attributes.ATTACK_DAMAGE);
+        float dmg = (float)io.github.adrielorihuela.legacyfolia.combat.Combat.attackDamage(this); // LegacyFolia - 1.8 weapon damage
         ItemStack weaponItem = this.getWeaponItem();
         DamageSource damageSource = weaponItem.getDamageSource(this);
         dmg = EnchantmentHelper.modifyDamage(level, weaponItem, target, damageSource, dmg);
